---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={"The Spy Guitar — History, Compatibility and a Modern Rebuild — Auspicious Music"}
  description={"A historical resource published on this domain between 2013 and 2017, documented with its current status, rights position and a tested modern alternative."}
  canonicalPath={"/legacy/the-spy-guitar/"}
  lang={"en"}
  noindex={false}
  loadStringField={false}
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<style is:global>
@layer components {
  /* Legacy pages open on graphite. That single inversion is what separates
     the archive from current editorial at a glance, before any label is read. */
  .lg-head { padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem) clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.5rem); }
  .lg-head .crumbs { color: var(--dark-muted); }
  .lg-head .crumbs a:hover { color: var(--dark-text); }
  .lg-head h1 { max-width: 15ch; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .lg-head .lede { margin-top: 1.5rem; max-width: 56ch; }

  .lg-flag {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta);
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); color: var(--ember-on-dark);
    padding-left: 0.875rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--ember-on-dark);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .lg-facts {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    display: grid; gap: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--dark-line);
  }
  .lg-facts > div {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(8rem, 12rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem; padding-block: 0.875rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--dark-line-soft);
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta);
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .lg-facts dt { color: var(--dark-muted); }
  .lg-facts dd { color: var(--dark-text); }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .lg-facts > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.1875rem; } }

  /* Status is stated once, large, and never dressed as a button */
  .lg-status {
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    margin-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    padding-top: 1.75rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--dark-line);
  }
  .lg-status strong {
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 1.05rem + 0.8vw, 1.625rem);
    font-weight: 550; letter-spacing: -0.014em;
  }
  .lg-status p { color: var(--dark-muted); font-size: 1rem; max-width: 50ch; line-height: 1.6; }

  /* body */
  .lg-body { max-width: var(--measure); }
  .lg-body > * + * { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .lg-body h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.2rem + 1.2vw, 2rem); letter-spacing: -0.016em;
    margin-top: clamp(2.75rem, 5vw, 3.75rem);
  }
  .lg-body p { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .lg-body a:not(.link) {
    color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .rights {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--line-strong);
    padding: 0.25rem 0 0.25rem 1.5rem;
  }
  .rights strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .rights p { color: var(--ink); font-size: 1.0625rem; }

  /* alternative — the one forward-looking action on the page */
  .alt {
    display: grid; gap: 1.5rem 3rem; align-items: center;
    padding: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  @media (min-width: 800px) { .alt { grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) auto; } }
  .alt h3 { font-size: 1.375rem; letter-spacing: -0.014em; }
  .alt p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1rem; margin-top: 0.5rem; max-width: 52ch; line-height: 1.6; }

  /* change log */
  .timeline { position: relative; padding-left: 2rem; }
  .timeline::before {
    content: ""; position: absolute; left: 3px; top: 1.2rem; bottom: 1.2rem;
    width: 1px; background: var(--line-strong);
  }
  .timeline li { position: relative; padding-block: 1.125rem; }
  .timeline li + li { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .timeline li::before {
    content: ""; position: absolute; left: -2rem; top: 1.7rem;
    inline-size: 7px; block-size: 7px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--canvas); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--line-strong);
  }
  .timeline li:last-child::before { background: var(--ember-bright); box-shadow: none; }
  .timeline time {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta);
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); color: var(--muted);
    display: block; margin-bottom: 0.375rem;
  }
  .timeline p { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 58ch; }

  .sources li { color: var(--muted); }
  .sources a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
}
</style>
</Fragment>

<main id="content">

  <article>
    <header class="band-dark lg-head" data-od-id="legacy-head">
      <div class="shell">
        <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <ol>
            <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
            <li><a href="/download/">Archive</a></li>
            <li>The Spy Guitar</li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <p class="lg-flag" style="margin-top:1.75rem">
          Historical resource<br>Independent relaunch under new ownership
        </p>

        <h1>The Spy Guitar</h1>

        <p class="lede">
          An Ableton sampler instrument published on this domain between 2013 and 2017
          by the former operator. This page documents what it was, what remains
          verifiable, and how the same result is built today.
        </p>

        <dl class="lg-facts">
          <div><dt>Historical period</dt><dd>2013 – 2017</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Former operator</dt><dd>Previous owner of this domain</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Original format</dt><dd>Ableton Live Pack / sampler instrument</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Rights status</dt><dd>Unverified — not licensed to the current publisher</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Verified externally</dt><dd>Yes — see sources</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Page reviewed</dt><dd>August 2026</dd></div>
        </dl>

        <div class="lg-status">
          <span class="status" data-state="unavailable" style="font-size:var(--t-meta)"></span>
          <div>
            <strong>Download unavailable</strong>
            <p>The original files were not transferred with the domain and their licence
               position is unresolved. Nothing is offered here that the current publisher
               does not hold the right to distribute.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="shell band">
      <div class="lg-body" data-od-id="legacy-body">

        <h2 style="margin-top:0">What the original project was</h2>
        <p>
          The Spy Guitar was a sampled electric guitar instrument for Ableton Live,
          built around a heavily processed clean tone and distributed as a free Live Pack
          from this domain. It was released alongside a visualiser project and promoted
          through the Ableton and controller communities of the period.
        </p>
        <p>
          It belongs to a specific moment: the years when Max for Live and free
          community Live Packs were how producers discovered each other's work, before
          that traffic moved to marketplaces and video platforms.
        </p>

        <h2>Why external sources still point here</h2>
        <p>
          The instrument was covered by production blogs and referenced in controller
          mapping communities, and several of those pages are still online and still
          linking to this address. That is the reason this URL returns a page rather
          than a redirect: the incoming intent is specific, and answering it with the
          homepage would be a worse outcome than answering it honestly.
        </p>

        <h2>What is still verifiable today</h2>
        <p>
          The archived pages, the external coverage, and the announcement history are
          all documented and independently checkable — those are listed under sources
          below. What is <em>not</em> verifiable is the current licence position of the
          audio content and the instrument files themselves, which is why they are not
          reissued here in any form.
        </p>

        <div class="rights">
          <strong>Rights and attribution</strong>
          <p>
            The Spy Guitar was created and published by the former operator of this
            domain. Auspicious Music is an independent publication under new ownership
            since 2026 and makes no claim to the original work, its authorship, or any
            associated credits. Nothing on this page should be read as a continuation of,
            or endorsement by, the former operator.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2>A modern alternative</h2>
        <p>
          The technique behind the original instrument is entirely reproducible, and
          more transparently than it was in 2013. The current guide walks through
          recording, looping and mapping a sampled instrument in Live 12 from scratch —
          with source audio you record yourself, so the licence question never arises.
        </p>

        <div class="alt" style="margin-top:2rem">
          <div>
            <h3>How to Build a Sampled Instrument in Ableton Live</h3>
            <p>Tested build, Live 12 and Sampler, with the failure points documented rather than edited out.</p>
          </div>
          <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/sound-design/sampled-instruments/building-a-sampled-instrument/">Read the guide</a>
        </div>

        <h2>Change log</h2>
        <ul class="timeline" data-reveal-group>
          <li data-reveal>
            <time datetime="2013">2013</time>
            <p>Instrument announced and published by the former operator on this domain.</p>
          </li>
          <li data-reveal>
            <time datetime="2017">2017</time>
            <p>Last archived capture of the original download page. The site stops being maintained shortly afterwards.</p>
          </li>
          <li data-reveal>
            <time datetime="2026-02">February 2026</time>
            <p>Domain acquired by the current publisher. Historic paths audited against archive records and backlink data.</p>
          </li>
          <li data-reveal>
            <time datetime="2026-08">August 2026</time>
            <p>This page published as a documented historical resource. Rights position recorded as unresolved; no files redistributed.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <section class="sources">
          <h2>Sources and original references</h2>
          <ol>
            <li>Internet Archive Wayback Machine — captures of this domain, 2013 to 2017.</li>
            <li>Contemporary production-blog coverage of the original release. Links retained in the internal URL registry.</li>
            <li><a href="https://maps.djtechtools.com/mappings/2929" rel="noopener">DJ TechTools mapping archive</a> — the related controller project, still maintained by its own publisher.</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <section data-od-id="relaunch-notice">
    <div class="shell relaunch">
      <p>Auspicious Music was relaunched under new ownership in 2026. Historical
         references are preserved for context.</p>
      <a class="link" href="/about/history-and-relaunch/">Read the history and relaunch note
        <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>
</BaseLayout>